I stand outside the dressing room.
There is a small rack there.
There is a very beautiful top on it.
It is a bright yellow top.
I like that yellow top.
I take it.
I try that on too.
That top fits me well.
It is very comfortable to wear.
I look at its price.
I do not see the price there.
I ask a staff member nearby.
"How many rupees for this top?" I ask her.
"Two thousand rupees, madam," she replies.
Two thousand rupees!
That is a big price.
I do not want this top.
I am not buying it.
I put that yellow top back on the rack.
